Run node containers/generate-seccomp.mjs to reproduce seccomp_profile.json.
The generator proves the entire Playwright profile equals the original Docker baseline plus exactly
an unconditional SCMP_ACT_ALLOW for clone, setns, unshare (empty args/includes/excludes).
It applies that proven delta plus an explicit SEC-014 chroot allow; all other default rules are preserved.
Allowing chroot grants no capability: the kernel still requires CAP_SYS_CHROOT in the caller's user namespace.
The cap-dropped non-root container process gets EPERM; Chromium can shrink its own namespace filesystem.
The Docker suite checks both this EPERM denial and Chromium startup with chromiumSandbox:true.
This avoids the historical profile's runc 1.5.2/libpathrs 0.2.6 initialization crash without disabling seccomp.
Profile and input hashes are recorded in seccomp/provenance.json and each images.lock.json entry.

M0 runner image tooling
Until the M1 protocol harness is available, build.mjs stages forwarder/tooling.js as dist/harness.js.
This entrypoint starts the TCP-to-unix forwarder and runs the supplied verification command.
It is test harness tooling, not an execution harness: no command returns CAPABILITY_UNAVAILABLE (M1).
The Python layout likewise refuses execution until its M1 protocol adapter replaces harness.py.
Images install no runtime dependencies and attempts must never invoke npm, pip or uv installers.
Build contexts are staged under the OS temporary directory and deleted even on build failure.
Build input hashes cover every staged file (including dependency contents and Dockerfile), with sorted relative paths and length-delimited framing.
